{
  "id": "ai4sgPipeline001",
  "name": "AI4SG · A Pipeline (overview)",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A · AI4SG Pipeline (overview)\n**Expert skills in → search → extract → human audit.** The two experts deliver two Markdown files; everything else is plumbing.\nRow 1 runs daily: find sources with the Search Skill, then read and interpret each new source with the Extraction Skill. Row 2 is the audit page where experts check every AI result against its source.",
        "width": 2420,
        "height": 110
      },
      "id": "9670078e-e763-5faf-9a02-aea6614cfe04",
      "name": "Note · title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 🧑‍🔬 Expert deliverables (the interface)\n`skills/search/SKILL.md`: what counts as AI for Social Good; focus countries and their languages (e.g. Bangladesh: bn, en; Indonesia: id, en; Thailand: th, en; India: hi, bn, ta, en); source types; local-language keywords, trusted sites, what to exclude.\n\n`skills/extraction/SKILL.md`: the fields to extract and how to judge them (e.g. cost, benefit, beneficiaries, strength of evidence), with worked examples.\n\nEdit a file → the next run uses it.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 410,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "838e98b1-6dcf-566c-a9b8-d9c730401e6d",
      "name": "Skill interface",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -270
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Search\nOne Search Agent run per country × language × source type (see workflow B).",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 250,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3b3923d9-e956-59b1-8fbf-059ca2dbedfb",
      "name": "Search",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        760,
        -110
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Extract\nOnly sources not seen before are read. The Extraction Skill is the prompt; every field must quote the source. Results are saved as *pending review*.",
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 250,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "036916ed-699b-5259-9a96-3a508307722e",
      "name": "Extract",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1260,
        -110
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "6da71642-add0-571d-95ee-30427244fe3c",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "21f5e1ed-acc1-5e83-8e89-61df3db979cf",
      "name": "Daily 06:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "fileSelector": "/skills/*/SKILL.md",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "b3ed40d3-7a8f-5ec6-b23d-d862ab3cc47c",
      "name": "Load Expert Skills",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.readWriteFile",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        20
      ],
      "executeOnce": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "text",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "de6342b5-a7dd-560d-a3f4-874838241d4d",
      "name": "Skills to Text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.extractFromFile",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Pair each skill text with its folder name, then expand the Search Skill's coverage block into tasks\nconst files = $('Load Expert Skills').all();\nconst skills = {};\n$input.all().forEach((it, i) => { skills[files[i].binary.data.directory.split('/').pop()] = it.json.data; });\nconst block = skills.search.match(/```json coverage\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)```/);\nconst cov = JSON.parse(block[1]);   // {countries:[{name, languages:[..]}], source_types:[..], max_tasks_per_run}\nconst tasks = [];\nfor (const c of cov.countries) for (const language of c.languages) for (const source_type of cov.source_types)\n  tasks.push({ country: c.name, language, source_type, search_skill: skills.search, extraction_skill: skills.extraction });\nreturn tasks.slice(0, cov.max_tasks_per_run || 40).map((json) => ({ json }));\n"
      },
      "id": "be20d996-8f7e-5606-b680-4c1ee5f438a9",
      "name": "Plan Search Tasks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        800,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "ai4sgSearchAgt01"
        },
        "mode": "each",
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "search_skill": "={{ $json.search_skill }}",
            "country": "={{ $json.country }}",
            "language": "={{ $json.language }}",
            "source_type": "={{ $json.source_type }}"
          },
          "schema": [
            {
              "id": "search_skill",
              "displayName": "search_skill",
              "type": "string",
              "display": true,
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true
            },
            {
              "id": "country",
              "displayName": "country",
              "type": "string",
              "display": true,
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true
            },
            {
              "id": "language",
              "displayName": "language",
              "type": "string",
              "display": true,
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true
            },
            {
              "id": "source_type",
              "displayName": "source_type",
              "type": "string",
              "display": true,
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "waitForSubWorkflow": true
        }
      },
      "id": "d0ee4a9e-7eb3-5867-ad5d-4588a1b6f6ad",
      "name": "Run Search Agent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1020,
        20
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "INSERT INTO sources (url, url_norm, title, source_type, country, language, why_relevant)\nSELECT url, url_norm, title, source_type, country, language, why_relevant\nFROM jsonb_to_recordset($1::jsonb) AS r(url text, url_norm text, title text, source_type text,\n                                        country text, language text, why_relevant text)\nON CONFLICT (url_norm) DO NOTHING\nRETURNING id, url, title, country, language",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [ JSON.stringify($input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(c => c.url_norm)) ] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "cee92238-e2ab-56fb-b24b-ab2097b73fcd",
      "name": "Save New Sources",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        1300,
        20
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "ai4sgPostgres001",
          "name": "AI4SG Postgres"
        }
      },
      "executeOnce": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "=https://r.jina.ai/{{ $json.url }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 90000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "text",
              "outputPropertyName": "text"
            }
          },
          "batching": {
            "batch": {
              "batchSize": 2,
              "batchInterval": 1000
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "31a16c1d-e6fa-5424-ba8b-2d0e1058c296",
      "name": "Fetch Full Text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1520,
        20
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $('Plan Search Tasks').first().json.extraction_skill }}\n\nReturn one JSON object with the fields defined above. For every field, include the supporting quote in the original language and its English translation.\n\n## Source\nURL: {{ $('Save New Sources').item.json.url }}\nCountry: {{ $('Save New Sources').item.json.country }}\n\n{{ ($json.text || '').slice(0, 40000) }}"
      },
      "id": "50b97ae5-6b12-5900-9097-5132451b73a6",
      "name": "Extract with Skill",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        1740,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "gpt-4o"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0
        }
      },
      "id": "636adb85-47e1-5b30-85ed-58dbd257b11a",
      "name": "LLM",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1740,
        240
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "ai4sgOpenAiApi01",
          "name": "AI4SG LLM (OpenAI-compatible)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((it, i) => {\n  const raw = String(it.json.text || '').replace(/^```(?:json)?\\s*|\\s*```$/g, '');\n  let fields = null; try { fields = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) {}\n  return { json: { source_id: $('Save New Sources').all()[i].json.id, fields, raw: fields ? null : raw } };\n});\n"
      },
      "id": "6a15cf8c-e019-5c75-b7d2-c3826eae0041",
      "name": "Parse JSON",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2000,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "INSERT INTO extractions (source_id, fields, raw_output, status) VALUES ($1, $2::jsonb, $3, 'pending_review')",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [ $json.source_id, JSON.stringify($json.fields), $json.raw ] }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "be2fa119-e2be-581b-a0ae-37f46b20bc94",
      "name": "Save for Review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        2220,
        20
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "ai4sgPostgres001",
          "name": "AI4SG Postgres"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 🧑‍🔬 Audit page (MVP front end): GET /webhook/ai4sg\nLists AI results next to their source link and quotes, newest first, so experts can check quality and correctness. Read-only for the MVP.",
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 250,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "3865b736-d578-5a43-bcd5-c087fa4a8bc5",
      "name": "Audit",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "GET",
        "path": "ai4sg",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "bd7303b7-deec-5bcd-b9c3-2873cfde6c35",
      "name": "Audit Page",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        520
      ],
      "webhookId": "e071918c-30e4-54e2-96e7-776f76da9bb7"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT e.id, e.fields, e.status, e.created_at, s.url, s.title, s.country, s.language, s.source_type\nFROM extractions e JOIN sources s ON s.id = e.source_id ORDER BY e.created_at DESC LIMIT 300",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "cb574d07-bf61-536f-be8a-5ccd09eb4e21",
      "name": "Load Results",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        240,
        520
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "ai4sgPostgres001",
          "name": "AI4SG Postgres"
        }
      },
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One card per result: extracted fields, quotes, link to the source\nconst rows = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r.id);\nconst esc = (s) => String(s ?? '').replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;' }[c]));\nconst cards = rows.map(r => `<article><h3><a href=\"${esc(r.url)}\" target=\"_blank\">${esc(r.title || r.url)}</a></h3>\n  <p>${esc(r.country)} · ${esc(r.language)} · ${esc(r.source_type)} · ${esc(r.status)}</p>\n  <pre>${esc(JSON.stringify(r.fields, null, 2))}</pre></article>`).join('');\nreturn [{ json: { body: `<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>AI4SG Audit</title>\n  <style>body{font:14px system-ui;max-width:960px;margin:24px auto;padding:0 16px}article{border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;margin:12px 0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}</style>\n  <h1>AI4SG · results to audit (${rows.length})</h1>${cards}` } }];\n"
      },
      "id": "54b4bb2e-56a5-5ba7-b06e-ad3a20d570f0",
      "name": "Render Page",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "text",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json.body }}",
        "options": {
          "responseHeaders": {
            "entries": [
              {
                "name": "Content-Type",
                "value": "text/html; charset=utf-8"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "e377154b-498e-5221-a46d-adc7f621555e",
      "name": "Respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        720,
        520
      ]
    }
  ],
